  "title": "Carol of the Bells",
  "composer": "Mykola Leontovych",
  "about": "Shchedryk is a Ukrainian New Year song, and its name comes from Bountiful Evening. Mykola Leontovych, a Ukrainian composer, conductor and teacher, built it on a four-note figure in 3/4 time. It was first sung on 29 December 1916 in Kyiv. Peter J. Wilhousky later made it the English Carol of the Bells.",
  "funFact": "Wilhousky gave it words about bells because the melody reminded him of handbells.",
